course: dictionary
lesson: 12460
title: Standing up with defiantly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Defiantly is an adverb: it tells you how someone does something. It means in a way that shows you refuse to obey, or that you openly stand up against someone or something. Look at the words around it for clues. «The girl said no to the bully, and she did it defiantly.» Saying no to a bully shows she is not giving in.
explain: The same word can show bravery or rudeness, depending on the story. «The knight raised his sword defiantly against the tyrant» shows courage, because he stands up to unfairness. «The pupil answered defiantly when the teacher asked him to sit down» shows he is refusing to do as asked. Read what happens next to decide which one it is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «she lifted her chin openly against the bully» instead of «she lifted her chin defiantly». It still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Phrases like «stare defiantly» and «answer defiantly» are useful clues too.
fact: Defiantly means in a way that shows you refuse to obey or openly stand up against someone or something.
fact: Defiantly is an adverb: it tells you how an action is done.
fact: «She lifted her chin defiantly» shows she is not giving in.
fact: Defiantly can show bravery when someone stands up to unfairness, or rudeness when someone refuses to do as asked.
fact: Context clues, such as the words around it and what happens next, help you decide which one the author means.
exercise: «The boy looked at the bully and said no, defiantly.» What does defiantly mean here? | In a happy, giggling way | *In a way that shows he refuses to give in | In a quiet, shy way | In a sleepy, slow way
exercise: «The mouse stood defiantly in front of the big cat to guard its babies.» Why did the mouse act defiantly? | To go to sleep | To run away as fast as it could | To ask the cat for a snack | *To stand up against the cat
exercise: Mia answers defiantly when her mum asks her to tidy up. What does answered defiantly suggest? | She is delighted to help | She is too tired to speak | She is lost and confused | *She refuses to do as she is asked
test: «The team kept playing defiantly, even when the rain got heavier.» What does defiantly suggest? | They played very slowly | They went home early | They were sad and tired | *They refused to give up
test: Which phrase shows someone openly standing up against something? | walk slowly home | sleep defiantly | sing softly | *stare defiantly
exam: Jayden reads «The little girl faced the tyrant defiantly.» Is she brave, rude, or both? What clue helps you decide? | Rude, because she is a girl | *Brave, because she stands up to a tyrant who is treating people unfairly | Sleepy, because she is little | Lost, because she is facing the wrong way
